diff --git a/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md b/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
--- a/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
+++ b/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
@@ -650,6 +650,12 @@
   persists a boot intent before its only start attempt, returns durable success
   receipts on retries and inspects the exact execution after a lost reply.
   Ordinary create routes cannot boot prepared resources before activation.
+  If the immutable startup lease expires before boot intent, the host durably
+  fences that destination as expired, deletes its private and published disk
+  copies, and returns an identity-bound terminal result. Only that result allows
+  the API to mark the operation failed and release pins/capacity. A lost cleanup
+  reply is retried against the same receipt. Expiry after boot intent is never
+  treated as proof of absence or permission to start another guest.
   Unknown boot outcomes retain their disk reservation and require reconciliation;
   registry absence is not a stop receipt. Source revocation and one-use enrollment
   authorization remain the calling coordinator's responsibility. Failed-start
